  "notes": "Peer-reviewed CDLB research Work published 2003-02-24. The live HTML reports version 2003-02-24 and the publisher PDF version 2003-02-25. It argues from orientation-bearing objects and pisan-dub-ba attachment morphology toward a later cuneiform direction change. Its decisive tag evidence is Ur III and Old Babylonian comparative evidence, not a direct Late Uruk proto-cuneiform observation. No Expression, Edition, Item, article payload, artifact, image, spatial annotation, orientation claim, semantic claim, or redistribution action is admitted.",
